summary": "{\"nodes\": [{\"distinct_partners\": 4, \"events\": 4, \"node\": 729}, {\"distinct_partners\": 2, \"events\": 2, \"node\": 1038}, {\"distinct_partners\": 5, \"events\": 5, \"node\": 1209}, {\"distinct_partners\": 3, \"events\": 3, \"node\": 66}, {\"distinct_partners\": 2, \"events\": 2, \"node\": 1429}], \"window\": [59001, 71500]}", "latency_ms": 7, "tokens_before": 60907, "tokens_after": 60907, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_6e649c32", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1010, 883], "window": [56117, 84917], "confidence": 0.65, "narrative": "No time-respecting 600-unit-gap chain can link 1010 to 883. Their 2-hop neighbourhoods are disjoint; the shortest time-ignoring route is ~5 hops through generic hubs (66/1688/582/1209), which caps any valid cascade span at ~2400 units. 1010 fires only twice (~59001-59717 and ~69901-70517) and 883 three times (~63318-64500, ~70518-71500, ~72501-74117). The first pairing is separated by >3600 units (infeasible); the second is temporally close but the required four intermediaries show almost no activity in that slot (66: 2 events, 1429: 0), so no ordered relay sequence exists. The static connection and the busy global window are hub artefacts, not evidence of propagation.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure (time-ignored):** 1010's 2-hop neighbourhood [step_03] is a small closed cluster {31, 66, 380, 499, 605, 999, 1010, 1429, 1688, 1824, 1952}; 883's 2-hop neighbourhood [step_07] is a disjoint set {149, 296, 356, 487, 582, 729, 971, 1038, 1090, 1209, 1343, 1542, 1561, 1600, 1937, 1951}. They only meet at 3-hop depth [step_06, step_12] via hubs (582, 1688, 158, 1542) \u2014 so the shortest possible route is \u22485 hops (e.g. 1010\u201366\u20131688\u2013582\u20131209\u2013883), and even that is not directionally consistent.\n\n**Temporal feasibility:** Both endpoints are extremely sparse. 1010 has exactly 2 events in the whole 28 800-unit window and 883 has 3 [step_02]. Bisection localises them:\n- 1010: one event in [59001, 59717], one in [69901, 70517] [step_08, step_10, step_13]\n- 883: events in [63318, 64500], [70518, 71500], [72501, 74117] [step_09, step_11, step_14]\n\nWith a \u22655-hop path, a 600-unit-per-hop chain can span at most ~2400 units. From 1010's first event (\u226459717) to 883's first event (\u226563318) the gap is \u22653601 \u2014 infeasible. The second 1010 event (~69901\u201370517) is close in time to 883's event (~70518\u201371500), but bridging them still requires four intermediaries (66 \u2192 1688 \u2192 582 \u2192 1209) each firing in strict order inside that ~1000\u20131600 unit slot. Intermediary activity is far too thin to support this: 66 has only 2 events in [69901, 71117] [step_15], and 1429 has none; over the much wider window [59001, 71500] the candidate relays 729/1038/1209/66/1429 total only 4/2/5/3/2 events with no repeats [step_16].\n\n**Confounder controls:** The window is busy overall (5330 events, 1854 active nodes [step_01]), and a time-ignored connection does exist [step_06, step_12] \u2014 but both are explained by hub nodes (158, 1542, 582, 1688) rather than by any ordered chain touching 1010. The near-coincidence in time of 1010's and 883's second events [step_13, step_14] is likewise not backed by relay activity [step_15, step_16].\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_6e649c32\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883],\n  \"window\": [56117, 84917],\n  \"confidence\": 0.65,\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting 600-unit-gap chain can link 1010 to 883. Their 2-hop neighbourhoods are disjoint; the shortest time-ignoring route is ~5 hops through generic hubs (66/1688/582/1209), which caps any valid cascade span at ~2400 units. 1010 fires only twice (~59001-59717 and ~69901-70517) and 883 three times (~63318-64500, ~70518-71500, ~72501-74117). The first pairing is separated by >3600 units (infeasible); the second is temporally close but the required four intermediaries show almost no activity in that slot (66: 2 events, 1429: 0), so no ordered relay sequence exists. The static connection and the busy global window are hub artefacts, not evidence of propagation.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 73485, "total_output_tokens": 9848, "total_tokens": 83333, "total_latency_ms": 133993, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}